{
  "rationale": "The plant separates sensing and motion: G1 models the robot's perception of obstacles, G2 models its motion commands. The specifications E1-E4 bind perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforce conservative recovery, and ensure alternation between random_walk and move_forward for coverage. Obstacle events always force a turn or scan before returning to exploration. Exploration alternates between random_walk and short forward pulses, with recovery turns on obstacle detection.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception (G1) and motion (G2) to allow modular specification.",
    "Specifications bind each perception outcome to exactly one safe controllable action, enforce conservative recovery, and maximize exploration progress by alternating random_walk and move_forward."
  ],
